<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <DUT Name="T_HashTableEntry" Id="{981738f9-cdaa-4fe1-95f5-e01133a08af9}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(* T_HashTableEntry - one node of a PMPS fixed-size hash table: a 32-bit search
key plus a pointer to the payload stored under that key.
A. Wallace 2019-09-16

Purpose:
    Give the PMPS pools an entry type for the TwinCAT Tc2_Utilities hash table
    helpers (F_CreateHashTableHnd / FB_HashTableCtrl), which address nodes by a
    32-bit key and an opaque value slot. The type lets each pool keep its
    payloads in its own statically allocated dataPool array and store only a
    pointer here, instead of copying whole payload structs into the table.

Usage:
    Internal to the PMPS library. FB_BeamParamAssertionPool and
    FB_LinearDeviceStateTable each declare

        entries : ARRAY[...] OF T_HashTableEntry

    as a static local, initialise it from their A_Reset action with
    F_CreateHashTableHnd( ADR( entries ), SIZEOF( entries ), hTable ), and then
    drive FB_HashTableCtrl (A_Add, A_Lookup, A_Remove, A_GetFirst, A_GetNext,
    A_Count, A_GetIndexAtPosPtr) over it. The putPosPtr / getPosPtr parameters
    of those blocks and actions are POINTER TO T_HashTableEntry, i.e. a node of
    this array; nothing else reads or writes the struct directly.

    Each pool's A_Add action inserts in two passes: the first A_Add reserves a
    node with a placeholder value, A_GetIndexAtPosPtr reports that node's index
    into entries, the caller copies its payload into dataPool[that index], and
    the second A_Add stores ADR( dataPool[that index] ) as the node's value.

Objectives:
    - The table moves no payload bytes: it holds a key and a pointer only. The
      owning FB's actions copy the referenced dataPool row into their getValue
      output when they hand a payload back to the caller.
    - The node stays at one key plus one pointer, so a pool sized from the
      PMPS_PARAM / PMPS_GVL limits keeps its node array small.
    - Only statically allocated storage is used, so table behaviour is
      deterministic and cannot fail at run time for lack of heap.

Caution: value is an unmanaged PVOID - see its comment below. The member order,
the member sizes and the pytmc pragma on key are carried into PMPS.tmc and the
pytmc-generated IOC, so do not reorder or resize members without regenerating
both.

History:
    2019-09-16 A. Wallace - type created with key, value and the Key pytmc
        pragma for the arbiter assertion pool (29eff94, "Working a bit on
        arbiter diagnostics").
    2019-11-21 .. 2020-06-26 A. Wallace - file relocated during the library
        reorganisation that ended in PMPS/DUTs/InternalDUT (d597bf0, ceaee6e,
        030f17c); declaration unchanged.
    2026-09-16 Y. Mandza - ProductVersion attribute removed (f77073f).
    2026-11-27 - header and per-member comments added; no member, type or
        layout change (DUT comment audit, task #371).
*)
TYPE T_HashTableEntry :
STRUCT
    // Search key of this node: unitless 32-bit identifier chosen by the
    // table owner, which the Tc2_Utilities hash table uses to find the node
    // (A_Lookup, A_Remove and A_Add take it as their key input).
    //   FB_BeamParamAssertionPool: the arbitration request ID that
    //       FB_Arbiter.AddRequest was given as nReqID (unique per device +
    //       state, never 0 and never PMPS_GVL.EXCLUDED_ASSERTION_ID).
    //   FB_LinearDeviceStateTable: the device state reference nStateRef
    //       passed to F_SetStateParams (also the lookup key for nSafeState
    //       and nTargetState in FB_LinearGovernor).
    // The pytmc pragma below declares it read-only as PV Key.
    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: Key
        io: i
     '}
    key : DWORD := 0;
    // Payload pointer belonging to key: the address of the owning FB's
    // dataPool row - ST_BP_ArbInternal in FB_BeamParamAssertionPool,
    // ST_DeviceState in FB_LinearDeviceStateTable. Not owned by this struct
    // or by the hash table: nothing here allocates, frees or NULL-checks
    // it. dataPool is a static array of the owning FB instance, so the
    // pointer is valid only while that instance exists and while the node
    // still holds the value; treat it as stale once the entry is removed or
    // the table is re-initialised. Until the second A_Add pass it holds a
    // placeholder (0 in FB_LinearDeviceStateTable, ADR(cstSafeBeam) in
    // FB_BeamParamAssertionPool). Unitless: dereference it as the owner's
    // payload type, never as T_HashTableEntry.
    value : PVOID := 0;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>